\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore economy unaffected by strong S$ - minister. \b0\par\par\uc2 221 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 25 (Reuter) - The recent strengthening of the Singapore dollar against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not affect the outlook for the domestic economy, Deputy Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong told Parliament. \par \par \uc2  "Overall, the value of the Singapore dollar has remained little changed measured against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's major trading partners and competitors," Lee said. \par \par \uc2  "The recent exchange rate movements are thus unlikely to have a significant impact on the Singapore economy as a whole," he said. \par \par \uc2  In the period from March 1 to April 30 the U.S. dollar depreciated by 3.8 percent against the Singapore dollar. In the same period, the Yen appreciated by 10.4 percent against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Lee said. \par \par \uc2  Lee said among local companies, exporters to the U.S. faced pressure on margins due to the weak greenback, but exporters to Europe and Japan were expected to benefit. \par \par \uc2  "The MAS (\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever necessary against exchange rate movements which are not supported by fundamentals," he said. \par \par \uc2  Lee added that the Government of Singapore Investment Corp (GIC), which manages Singapore's oficial \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, had not suffered any major losses as a result of the exchange rate movements. \par \par \uc2  -- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000