\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Taiwan dlr plunges, others steady. \b0\par\par\uc2 566 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 22 (Reuter) - The Taiwan dollar plunged against the U.S. dollar in mid-morning but other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were steady in quiet trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar tumbled on strong month-end U.S. dollar demand, falling to T$25.9250 after 105 minutes of trade, against Saturday's T$25.7280 close. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Taipei said Saturday's news of Taiwan's first-quarter balance of payments deficit triggered expectations of more Taiwan dollar falls. "Seeing that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not entered to stop the rate's plunges as it said it would, month-end U.S. dollar demand just emerged heavily," one said. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was quoted around 25.8155/00 at midday. \par \par \uc2  In other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. dollar's firmness against the yen and mark was seen supporting it against the Singapore dollar and Malaysian ringgit. \par \par \uc2  The dollar managed to stay above 87.00 yen at midday after a New York close at 86.80/90. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was quiet and range-bound against the greenback. It opened at 1.3937/40 and firmed to 1.3926 in late morning. At midday it was quoted around 1.3920/30. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. bank dealer in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar firmed above 1.3915. \par \par \uc2  "It's a level where they've \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past," he said. The authority does not normallt comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar should trade in a range of 1.3915/70 this week, the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit gained slightly against the dollar in thin early trade as players awaited fresh leads before taking positions, dealers in Kuala Lumpur said. \par \par \uc2  "There's some ringgit buying from Singapore but otherwise, not much interest is seen," said one dealer. He said the lack of activity also reflected the dollar's uncertainty against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0415 GMT, the ringgit was trading at 2.4625/35 to the dollar against 2.4655/65 at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  A Singapore dealer said foreign funds still wanted to sell the ringgit for U.S. dollars. "It's trending softer towards the top of 2.46, but I don't see it coming below 2.4600 for the short term. This week it will probably be 2.4600-2.4700." \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht was marginally firmer against the dollar in active early trading at 24.755-24.765, from Friday's 24.76. \par \par \uc2  But in Singapore trading, "the baht is surprisingly quiet, with nothing going on after last Friday's announcement of dissolution of parliament," a U.S. bank dealer in Singapore said. "The market doesn't seem to be too concerned about the political ramifications. They expect it will be business as usual." \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dealer described the Indonesian rupiah as "pretty dead." \par \par \uc2  "It's been around 2,229 all morning. Liquidity is a touch easier in the market. It's a very quiet morning. There's no discernible trend in anything. \par \par \uc2  "There's still investor interest coming in to sell dollars and buy the rupiah, but because of the easier liquidity situation, the market is tending to support the dollar at these levels. It's basically a Mexican standoff." \par \par \uc2  Rupiah was quoted at 2,228.75/9.50 at midday. \par \par \uc2  --Matthew Lewis (65-8703093) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr5m07lfn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
