\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Retreats From Record High After MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 1995\par 04:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar has recovered from record lows against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar set earlier Wednesday following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the U.S. unit by the local de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar hit a new low of at S$1.3905 around 0050 GMT, a move traders said came as the dollar also plunged to record lows against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar tumbled against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early Asian trading amid a bout of speculative selling, breaking through its previous record low of 80.18 yen to hit a low of 79.85 yen around 0026 GMT. \par \par \uc2  However, traders said, buying of the U.S. dollar around S$1.3907-10 by the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, helped the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebound from its lows to trade at S$1.3920 around 0244 GMT. However, the U.S. dollar is still down from levels around S$1.3953 seen late Tuesday in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The recovery of the U.S. dollar against the yen also helped lift the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  off its lows in the local market, traders said. The dollar recovered shortly after setting its new record low, to trade at 80.25 yen around 0244 GMT. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-04-95 \par \par \uc2  0247GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 \par \par \uc2 Dokument