\par\par \b \uc2  Hu says MAS keeps rein on Singapore dollar - paper. \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 17 (Reuter) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent months to stem the tide of money seeking refuge in Singapore, Finance Minister Richard Hu said in an interview with the Business Times. \par \par \uc2  "Singapore has attracted its share of safe haven money, which of course exerts upward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, and the MAS has had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  quite actively to support the U.S. dollar, not to allow the Singapore dollar to rise too rapidly," Hu told the paper. \par \par \uc2  However, Hu discounted the idea of having to take drastic action soon to curb the Singapore dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  "It hasn't reached that point yet," he said. "This is an unusual period because of the yen, but we don't expect the appreciation to continue indefinitely. The main impact isn't on the U.S., it's a Japanese problem," he said. \par \par \uc2  Hu said Singapore has to continue to curb the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation and the consequence of this was that it drives liquidity up and depresses interest rates. If this persists, it causes asset inflation, Hu said, adding that there was a need to balance the two effects. \par \par \uc2  He said Singapore would only use negative interest rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls as a last resort because of fears that meddling with such controls may hurt Singapore's reputation as a financial centre. \par \par \uc2  The finance minister said it was a costly exercise to fight speculators but declined to disclose how much money the MAS has pumped in so far to support the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  He noted that the Singapore-U.S. dollar exchange rate has not risen as fast as the yen-U.S. dollar rate. \par \par \uc2  -- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr4h08iis\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
