\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Sets Record;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1995\par 10:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar fell to a historic low against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  early Monday trading and is now higher after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said dealers. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following comments from an interview by a local paper with Finance Minister Richard Hu, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  Hu said: 'Singapore has attracted its share of safe haven money, which of course exerts upward pressure on the Singapore dollar, and the MAS (\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) has had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  quite actively to support the dollar, to not allow the Singapore dollar to rise too rapidly.' The MAS is the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Hu added that 'we have to continue to do this.' \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell to a new historic low of S$1.3920 at around 0015 GMT, said dealers, adding that there was strong support for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at those levels. \par \par \uc2  There was active buying of the U.S. dollar by the MAS between S$1.3920-30 Monday morning, said two traders, one from a local bank and another from a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst said Hu's statement 'implied that the Singapore dollar still has more room to rise.' Trading interest in the U.S. dollar against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to be thin for the rest of Monday in light of public holidays in U.K., Germany and France, he said. \par \par \uc2  Resistance for the dollar is likely to be around S$1.3965-70 while strong support is seen at S$1.3920. \par \par \uc2  Around 0830 GMT, the dollar was trading around S$1.3967, from S$1.3945 early in Asian trading and from S$1.3955 at about the same time on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 0.000%-0.125%, from 1.875%-2.000% Thursday. The 3-month interbank rate was at 1.875%-2.000%, from 2.250%-2.375% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-04-95 \par \par \uc2  0847GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr4h02ns7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
