\par\par \b \uc2  APEC/Singapore Fin Min -2: Will Continue To Support Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1995\par 06:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  'We are quite pleased with the outcome,' Hu said. 'There were two main issues we wanted to see addressed: why did the Mexican crisis occur and what is the effect of exchange-rate movements on the regional economies,' he said, adding that both of these subjects were discussed. \par \par \uc2  But Hu acknowledged that the precipitous fall of the dollar and the corresponding rise of the yen in recent months has affected some APEC members 'very seriously'. \par \par \uc2  Singapore has no yen-denominated debt and so has not suffered as much as many other countries, Hu noted. And Singapore manages its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , against which it has actually fallen since the beginning of the year because of its depreciation against the Japanese yen and Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  Still, as Hu spoke early Monday the dollar was hovering just above a record low set at 0005 GMT of S$1.3927, and the minister said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prevent speculators from pouring into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Hu said he and other APEC finance ministers pressured the U.S. and Japan at the weekend's summit to take action to stem the volatility in dollar-yen movements. \par \par \uc2  He acknowledged that only those two countries can solve the problem. 'That is a bilateral problem and there is very little the other APEC members can do except to exert a kind of moral suasion,' he said. \par \par \uc2  And ultimately, Hu said, the problem weighs more heavily on Japan than on the U.S. because Japan is getting hurt much more. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-04-95 \par \par \uc2  0438GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr4h02n3f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
