\par\par \b \uc2  Asian exotics seen doubtful of US dlr 'recovery'. \b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 6 (Reuter) - Dealers of Asian exotic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  doubt that the U.S. dollar has temporarily bottomed at around 86.00 yen and are unimpressed with Washington's efforts to drum up \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support for the greenback. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's longterm weakness "will not change until the U.S. changes monetary policy", said Ian Clague, managing director of global trading at Chemical Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "The pure fact of the matter is that monetary policy is too lax in the U.S. The Japanese have done what they can to alleviate the strength of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but really the source of the problem is with the U.S." \par \par \uc2  Clague said the U.S. must confront its huge budget and trade deficits in order to put the dollar on the path to permanent recovery. \par \par \uc2  Asian exotic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed against the dollar, led by a high-flying ringgit, which was buoyed by domestic election news. The ringgit opened firmer and is expected to track a wide range between 2.4900 and 2.5100 today. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Kuala Lumpur said buying interest was chiefly from offshore interbank players, although corporate buyers were also seen buying the ringgit against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "I know the ringgit looks like a one-way trend at the moment, but there is some possibility that Bank Negara might smooth the rise," said Clague. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was locked in at 1.4055/57 early on, but was still within striking distance of its historic high of 1.4030 on March 8. \par \par \uc2  "So far dollar-Sing has not reacted fully to the rise in the yen and the ringgit," said Clague. "I think Singapore interest rates should rise, and the reduction in the volume of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  also means there should be less liquidity in the money market." \par \par \uc2  In Jakarta, the rupiah extended its gains against the dollar in active trading on the back of sustained tight money market liquidity, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said operators were mainly busy filling the gaps in their rupiah liquidity positions, causing value today and tomorrow dollars to tumble in early trade. \par \par \uc2  Value today dollars fell to 2,222.75/2,223.25 rupiah from the opening of 2,224.50/25.50. Value tomorrow were last at 2,223.75/24.35. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore trading, the rupiah moved between 2,226.50 and 2,228.00 in the morning. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's interbank market is closed for a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr4608zbn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
