\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  firmer, eye on Fed  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , April 3 (Reuter) - Exotic Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed against the U.S. dollar but stayed within tight bands as players waited to see if the dollar's slide would be halted by U.S. Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asian time, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said sentiment for the dollar remains bearish despite the moves by the BUBA to cut German interest rates and by the BOJ to support the dollar against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "The main points of interest this morning are (Indonesian) rupiah and (Thai) baht," said Ian Clague, managing director of global trading at Chemical Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  He said the dollar's weakness against the yen and mark prompted a 10-satang increase in the dollar/baht midrate from Friday. \par \par \uc2  For the rupiah, the market is watching to see if Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to trade at the top end of its band. \par \par \uc2  In early Thai trade, the baht firmed against the midrate and traded in a narrow band in morning dealings on offshore selling of the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Spot baht ranged 24.635-24.640 to the dollar, up from an earlier 24.635-24.655, said a Citibank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The midrate was fixed 10 satang higher at 24.64 to the dollar from Friday when the baht ended at 24.64-24.65. \par \par \uc2  There was some baht traded at value today at 24.62875, he said. \par \par \uc2  The swap market was thin and mainly corporate demand was sending premiums higher, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  Clague said the market interpreted the midrate increase as "quite positive." \par \par \uc2  "That increases confidence in the basket system," he said. \par \par \uc2  For the rupiah, Clague said that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could well be triggered at the 2,235.00 level. \par \par \uc2  "On Friday night we were trading above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, so there was some expectation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this morning, that hasn't happened so far. But it's still a strong possibility, because we're still trading right at the top level of the band." he said. \par \par \uc2  "The forwards are now discounting devaluation of the rupiah of over eight percent next year against an official target that looks like three or four percent. So we may have an announcement of that target and perhaps see some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forwards," Clague said. \par \par \uc2  In early Jakarta trade, the rupiah hovered below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower limit following early offshore dollar buying, dealers said. One private bank dealer said Singapore players became nervous after the dollar lost more ground against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "They dumped the rupiah and pushed up spot dollar, which hit 2,235.50 before the Jakarta market opened," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  But relatively tight money market liquidity urged local banks to unwind their dollar positions, keeping spot rupiah at 2,234.00/34.50 against the dollar at mid-morning. \par \par \uc2  Value tomorrow was last quoted at 2,233.50/34.00. \par \par \uc2  For the Singapore dollar, dealers said activity was quiet, although the unit firmed against the greenback to 1.4088/98 around midday. The Singapore dollar's all-time high, reached last month, is 1.4020/30. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit is seen in a range of 2.5200 to 2.5260 on Monday, dealers said. "There is some speculation that the reserve requirements of Malaysian banks might be raised," said Clague. "Bank Negara are looking for ways to reduce their liquidity in the money market, and this would be one way to do it." \par \par \uc2  --Singapore newsroom (65-8703080) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr43093zm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
