\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Rises Against Dlr; May Set New Record \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1995\par 10:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-DJ)--The U.S. broke out of its support for the dollar at S$1.4100 Monday in Asian trading. This occured amidst heavy selling against the Singapore dollar, said traders, adding that a new record may be set soon. \par \par \uc2  'There were very large sell orders for the dollar against the Sing unit,' said a trader at local bank. She said the dollar 'may very well test the historical low' in either late Asian trading or trading in Europe or the U.S. later today. \par \par \uc2  The trader said there are no particular reasons for the dollar's weakness against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit and noted a lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the local \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar hit a historical low of S$1.4030 on March 9 this year. \par \par \uc2  Other traders said the dollar's weakness against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due mainly to the spillover effect from the uncertainty the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the majors. 'Those who said that the dollar appeared weak against the mark and the yen, came into the market to sell the dollar against the Singapore,' said a trader at a Japanese bank here. \par \par \uc2  Most traders said the overall sentiment of the dollar against the Singapore unit is still bearish. 'The movement of the dollar against the majors tends to be a bit more choppy than the dollar against the Singapore unit,' said the trader at the local bank. \par \par \uc2  Around 0740 GMT, the dollar was trading around S$1.4087, from S$1.4115 early in Asian trading and from S$1.4175 at about the same time on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 2.750%-2.625%, from 3.500%-3.375% at about the same time Friday. \par \par \uc2  The 3-month interbank rate was at 2.875%-2.750%, from 2.875%-2.750%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-04-95 \par \par \uc2  0814GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr4302cud\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
