\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ has been buying dlrs via Singapore - traders. \b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 14 (Reuter) - The Bank of Japan (BOJ) has started using a new method of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of having a limited number of banks here discreetly buy dollars through U.S. and European banks in Singapore, traders here said. \par \par \uc2  The tactic, which is in addition to ordinary dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Tokyo market, is seen aimed at the banks in Singapore which apparently handle the orders of overseas hedge funds, a major driving force in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "The method is helping make the BOJ's action less visible in Tokyo, while leaving people here the impression that the dollar's bottom is strangely solid," said a Tokyo bank trader. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ customarily does not comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also occasionally bought dollars directly through banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or checked dollar/yen rates as a step preceding \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Tokyo traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ now seems keen to get to grips with the activity of overseas hedge funds, since Japanese investors' influence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has waned," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager. Hedge funds are highly leveraged investment trust funds, generally backed by a number of wealthy individuals. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo bank traders said the BOJ has been using its new method since last week, but volume so far has not been large. \par \par \uc2  The traders said the dollar's plunge against the yen last week apparently prompted the BOJ to adopt the method. \par \par \uc2  BOJ buying through this method tends to take place when the dollar is pushed down after a round of stop-loss sales, they said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has hovered around 90-92 yen since it plunged to a new global low of 88.75 yen last Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ is seen intent on keeping the dollar from falling below 90 yen, as a further dive of the dollar against the yen might force the BOJ to ease credit," said one Tokyo trader. Tokyo Treasury desk ---81-3-3432-1396 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011104dr3e00byp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
