\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore dollar ends at new high against US dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 6 (Reuter) - The Singapore dollar closed at a historical high of 1.4410/20 against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The high was triggered by last Friday's close at Singapore $1.4445, which wiped out the previous high in Asian time at S$1.4475/80 on January 23, and the London time previous high at S$1.4455 on January 23, a U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened today at 1.4430/35 and climbed to 1.4408 during the day. "It was given but not offered at 1.4408," said the dealer. \par \par \uc2  Trading was quiet for most of the afternoon, with the dollar stuck in the S$1.4410/20 range. \par \par \uc2  The greenback against the Singapore unit "came down in sympathy with the majors", the dealer said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities will likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the the unit breaks the 1.4400 level, traders said. "There's no clear commercial buying or selling at the moment. They are all worriedly following how the majors will do (overnight)." \par \par \uc2  Some traders expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore to step in at S$1.4430 today and were surprised when nothing happened. \par \par \uc2  -- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011104dr3600kmo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
