\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Softens Despite Broad Dlr Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 1995\par 10:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-DJ)--The dollar held its ground Wednesday against the Singapore dollar, actually gaining even as it softened during Asian trading against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar's broad weakness against the majors is mitigated by commercial interests buying back short-dollar positions they took late last year, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Also holding up the dollar is a general lack of trading interest in the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fear that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) lie just below current levels, some traders said. \par \par \uc2  In late-Asian trading around 0830 GMT, the dollar was trading around S$1.4532, from S$1.4518 early in Asian trading and from S$1.4522 at about the same time on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The MAS has been considered by \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers recently to be holding dollar-supportive positions just below S$1.4500 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Other traders, however, denied that fear of MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is keeping the dollar strong, arguing instead that a scramble to cover short positions taken late in 1994 is supporting the dollar, which is not expected to depreciate as quickly against the Singapore dollar in 1995. \par \par \uc2  'There's no fear of the MAS, it's just a matter of commercial interest to buy back the dollar-Sing they went short on last year,' said one local-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  'People don't want to be short the dollar at these very low levels,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Also holding the dollar from dropping against the Singapore dollar is the continuing gap between U.S. and Singapore interest rates, traders said. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 1.750%-1.625%, from 1.500%-1.375% at about the same time Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The 3-month interbank rate stood at 2.6875-2.5625%, from 2.625%-2.500%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 22-02-95 \par \par \uc2  0952GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr2m018x3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
